From 4018406b0f52726ab2e4db1d5685d0480bc9ebec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rmanish2000-del <rmanish2000@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 20:50:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] One palette for the whole site: the Prava family
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There were two, and they had drifted apart. src/styles/tokens.css — the file the
pages actually load — was blue-cast; src/design-system/tokens.css was green-cast
"Ink & Paper"; and /warrant, the console the site already hosts, was a third
thing again. A reader moving between a page, the gallery and the console saw
three products.

Both token files now carry identical values for every shared name, taken from
the console: warm off-white paper #faf9f7, near-black ink #171717, warm neutral
rules, and one teal primary #0f766e that is the link colour, the focus ring, the
primary fill and the design system's --verdigris at the same time. Controls take
the pill shape. The mono voice is a token now, --font-mono, and LedgerBadge stops
hardcoding its own stack.

Only the primary hue moves. Prava's own rule is that semantic colours "keep their
own colours: those are product semantics, not skin", so --iris still means
approved-design-intent and --saffron still means gated, in the hues a reader has
already learned. What was skin became teal; what was meaning stayed put.

Two parts of the console are deliberately NOT brought over, because rules here
outrank a borrowed look. Its elevation: `07` and the CL-2 test forbid an
elevation token and any box-shadow used for separation, so separation stays
borders and surfaces. Its web fonts: `08` §8 sets a zero font budget, so Inter
and IBM Plex Mono lead the stacks and are never fetched — a machine that has
them renders the console's type exactly, and a machine that does not gets the
system stack it got before.

The dark theme is the one part with no original, since the console is light-only.
It is derived rather than invented: the same warm cast inverted, and the accent
lifted to the teal the console uses on its own dark card.

Every colour was verified before it was written, with the gate's own maths, and
then by the gate: 78 design-system checks pass, including all 38 G-C1/G-C2
contrast pairs recomputed from the token file across both themes and both
background levels. Nothing sits near a floor — the tightest pair is
border-input against bg-subtle at 4.23:1 against a 3:1 minimum.

DS-D2 is re-recorded rather than satisfied. That gate hashes every built route to
catch a design-system change LEAKING into the site; here the site was changed on
purpose, so reverting would defeat the request and silence is not an option. The
recordedFrom field says exactly that.

/warrant is untouched.

Verified: ds:gates 78/78 · vitest 91/91 · html-validate clean · eslint clean ·
prettier clean · accessibility suite 250/250 across chromium-light and
chromium-dark · rendered page confirms paper, ink, Inter, teal, pill controls,
IBM Plex Mono, and no #1b4de4 anywhere.

